<p>The online shop <strong>epalinca.ro</strong> (the “Site”) is owned and operated by the company above (the “Seller”), producer of the spirits sold under the <strong>Zekulhyda</strong> brand.</p>

<h2>2. Definitions</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Consumer</strong> – any natural person acting for purposes outside their trade, business, craft or profession (Government Emergency Ordinance no. 34/2014 – “GEO 34/2014”; Government Ordinance no. 21/1992 – “GO 21/1992”).</li>
  <li><strong>Customer</strong> – the adult natural person or legal entity placing an order on the Site.</li>
  <li><strong>Order</strong> – the electronic document through which the Customer expresses the intention to purchase the selected products.</li>
  <li><strong>Distance contract</strong> – the contract concluded between the Seller and the Customer through the Site, without the simultaneous physical presence of the parties, within the meaning of GEO 34/2014.</li>
  <li><strong>Products</strong> – the spirits (pálinka, fruit distillates) and accessories offered for sale on the Site.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Acceptance of the terms</h2>
<p>By using the Site and placing an order you confirm that you have read, understood and fully accept these Terms and conditions, together with the <a href="{{ pages['politica-de-confidentialitate'].url }}">Privacy policy</a>, the <a href="{{ pages['politica-cookies'].url }}">Cookie policy</a>, <a href="{{ pages['livrare-si-plata'].url }}">Delivery and payment</a> and the <a href="{{ pages['politica-de-retur'].url }}">Returns policy</a>, which form an integral part of the contract. The Seller may update the Terms; the version applicable to an order is the one in force on the day the order is placed, which we provide to you on a durable medium (confirmation e-mail).</p>

<h2>4. Minimum age – 18 years</h2>
<p>The Site sells <strong>alcoholic beverages only</strong>. Under the applicable law (Law no. 61/1991, republished, and Law no. 148/2000 on advertising), the sale and delivery of alcoholic beverages to minors is <strong>prohibited</strong>. Therefore:</p>
<ul>
  <li>orders may only be placed by persons who are <strong>at least 18 years old</strong>; by confirming your age when entering the Site and by placing an order you declare, on your own responsibility, that you are of legal age;</li>
  <li>the parcel is handed over to an adult only; the courier may ask for an identity document and may refuse delivery if age cannot be verified – in that case the order is cancelled and the amounts paid are refunded, less the shipping cost actually incurred;</li>
  <li>the Seller reserves the right to refuse or cancel any order that can reasonably be assumed to have been placed by or for a minor.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Excessive alcohol consumption seriously harms your health.</strong> Do not drive under the influence of alcohol.</p>

<h2>5. Products and information</h2>
<p>The essential characteristics of the Products (name, category, alcohol content, net volume, producer, allergens where applicable) are shown on each product page and on the product label, in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1169/2011 on the provision of food information to consumers and Regulation (EU) 2019/787 on spirit drinks. Spirit drinks with an alcohol content of 10% vol. or more do not require a date of minimum durability.</p>
<p>Images are for illustration; batches may show slight differences in colour or labelling that do not affect the quality of the product. The Seller takes all reasonable care to keep the information accurate; however, obvious clerical or calculation errors are not binding on the Seller.</p>
<p>Product availability is displayed in real time on the Site. If an ordered product becomes unavailable, we will inform you as soon as possible and offer a replacement, postponement or cancellation of the order with a full refund.</p>

<h2>6. Prices</h2>
<p>All prices are in <strong>Romanian lei (RON)</strong> and <strong>include VAT</strong> and the excise duty applicable to alcoholic beverages under the Romanian Fiscal Code. Prices do not include delivery costs, which are shown separately before the order is completed (Art. 6 of GEO 34/2014). Where a price reduction is announced, we indicate the prior price, i.e. the lowest price applied in the 30 days before the reduction, in accordance with GO 21/1992 as amended by GO 58/2022.</p>
<p>The price displayed when the order is placed applies. The Seller may change prices at any time without affecting orders already confirmed.</p>

<h2>7. Placing the order and conclusion of the contract</h2>
<p>An order is placed by completing the checkout steps and pressing the button that explicitly indicates the obligation to pay (“Checkout” / “Pay”), as required by Art. 8 of GEO 34/2014. The order constitutes an offer to purchase. After placing it you automatically receive an e-mail acknowledging the order, in accordance with Law no. 365/2002 on electronic commerce.</p>
<p><strong>The contract is concluded</strong> when the Seller sends the dispatch confirmation, or, for card payments, when the payment is confirmed. The Seller may refuse or cancel an order, informing the Customer, in the following cases: product unavailability, obvious price or display errors, reasonable suspicion of fraud, inability to verify age, incomplete delivery details or repeated refusal of parcels.</p>

<h2>8. Payment and invoicing</h2>
<p>Payment can be made by the methods shown at checkout: <strong>bank card</strong> (processed securely by our partner payment processor; the Seller does not store card data) or <strong>cash on delivery</strong>, where available. No additional fee is charged for card payments.</p>
<p>An electronic invoice is issued for every order and sent to the e-mail address provided and, where required by law, transmitted through the Romanian national RO e-Factura system under Law no. 296/2023 and GEO no. 120/2021, as amended. By accepting these Terms you agree to receive the invoice in electronic form.</p>

<h2>9. Delivery</h2>
<p>Delivery is made by courier, within Romania only, to the address given in the order. The estimated delivery time is shown on the <a href="{{ pages['livrare-si-plata'].url }}">Delivery and payment</a> page; unless otherwise agreed, the Products are delivered within 30 days of the conclusion of the contract (Art. 18 of GEO 34/2014). The risk of loss or damage to the Products passes to the Customer when the Customer, or a third party designated by the Customer other than the carrier, takes physical possession of the Products (Art. 20 of GEO 34/2014).</p>
<p>We recommend checking the parcel on receipt, in the presence of the courier; any visible damage should be recorded in the courier’s report and reported to us as soon as possible at the e-mail address above. The Products are excise goods delivered in sealed packaging with the fiscal marking (tax strip) applied by the producer.</p>

<h2>10. Right of withdrawal (returns)</h2>
<p>As a consumer you have the right to withdraw from the contract <strong>without giving any reason within 14 calendar days</strong> from the day on which you, or a third party designated by you other than the carrier, take physical possession of the Products (Art. 9 of GEO 34/2014). To exercise this right, inform us by an unequivocal statement (e-mail to the address above, post, or the withdrawal form on the <a href="{{ pages['politica-de-retur'].url }}">Returns policy</a> page) before the deadline expires.</p>
<ul>
  <li>You must return the Products without undue delay and no later than 14 days from the day you communicate your withdrawal; <strong>the direct cost of returning</strong> the Products is borne by you (Art. 14).</li>
  <li>We refund all amounts received, including the cost of standard delivery, without undue delay and no later than 14 days from the day we are informed; we may withhold the refund until we have received the Products or proof that you have sent them (Art. 13).</li>
  <li>You are liable for any diminished value of the Products resulting from handling beyond what is necessary to establish their nature and characteristics.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Exception (Art. 16(e) of GEO 34/2014):</strong> the right of withdrawal <strong>does not apply</strong> to sealed Products which have been unsealed after delivery and cannot be returned for health protection or hygiene reasons. Bottles whose seal, capsule or tax strip has been opened or damaged cannot be returned, unless the Product is non-conforming.</p>

<h2>11. Conformity and legal guarantee</h2>
<p>The Seller is liable to the consumer for any lack of conformity existing at the time of delivery, under <strong>GEO no. 140/2021</strong> on certain aspects of contracts for the sale of goods, for a period of 2 years from delivery. In the event of a lack of conformity you are entitled, in the order set by law, to have the Products brought into conformity (replacement), to a proportionate price reduction or to termination of the contract, free of charge. A lack of conformity that becomes apparent within 12 months of delivery is presumed to have existed at the time of delivery, unless proven otherwise.</p>
<p>The following do not constitute a lack of conformity: the natural sediment of fruit distillates, natural colour variation between batches, or damage caused by improper storage (exposure to sunlight, extreme temperatures) after delivery.</p>

